    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d85">

                <pb facs="0123" n="49" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg49"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Burnley</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-01-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 19, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Referring to your note of the 13th instant,
                    in which you propose that the James Douglas may be brought to New York and there
                    regularly appraised and a settlement made with the owners, I have the honor to
                    enclose, in reply, a copy of a letter of the 31st ultimo from the Secretary of
                    the Navy.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>J. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hume Burnley,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d85-a1.xml" xpointer="d85-a1"/>
            </div>
